 ---
 
+## Testing and evaluation
+
+The project ships with an offline test suite and a RAG evaluation harness. Both run in `DEMO_MODE`, so they need no API key and cost nothing.
+
+```bash
+pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
+pytest --cov=app                      # 37 tests: guardrails, ingestion, retrieval, LLM path, CLI
+python -m app.ingest                  # build the index the evaluation reads
+python -m eval.run_eval               # retrieval + guardrail metrics on eval/golden_set.json
+```
+
+**Test suite (`tests/`).** Tests build their own FAISS index in a temporary folder, so they never modify `vectorstore/`. They cover Guardrail 1 (vague and punctuation-only queries), Guardrail 2 (threshold enforcement and the zero-vector case), metadata parsing and chunk sizes, and a grounding check that every candidate named in an answer comes from a cited source. The OpenAI generation path is tested with LangChain's `FakeListChatModel`, which verifies the prompt contents and the "Sorry, I cannot help" refusal contract without a network call.
+
+**Evaluation (`eval/`).** `golden_set.json` holds 18 labelled queries: 11 in-scope roles, 3 unclear requests, and 4 out-of-scope requests. `run_eval.py` reports:
+
+| Metric | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| Hit@1 / Hit@k / MRR | Whether the correct resume is retrieved, and how high it ranks |
+| Status accuracy | Share of queries that get the expected `matched` / `unclear` / `no_match` status |
+| Refusal precision | Of all refusals, how many were correct (the app did not refuse a valid request) |
+| Refusal recall | Of all requests that should be refused, how many were (the app did not answer out-of-scope requests) |
+
+Baseline in demo mode: Hit@1 1.00, MRR 1.00, status accuracy 0.94, refusal precision 1.00, refusal recall 0.86.
+
+**Known issue.** Case `oos-03` ("certified nurse for night shifts") is wrongly matched. Its only word in common with the library is "certified", and TF-IDF gives a single shared term a score (0.21) above the demo threshold (0.12). Possible fixes: add "certified" to the boilerplate stop words, or require at least two overlapping terms before trusting a demo-mode match.
+
+**CI.** `.github/workflows/tests.yml` runs the tests and the evaluation on every push and pull request. The evaluation acts as a quality gate: the build fails if status accuracy drops below 0.90 or Hit@k drops below 1.00. The JSON report is uploaded as a build artifact.
+
+Add `--json eval/report.json` to save results. With `DEMO_MODE=0` and an API key, the same harness scores the OpenAI embeddings and model.
+
+---
+
